//< A `{ … }` standing as a statement of its own is refused, not taken without a word
//<
//< **A block with no heading cannot be told from a continuation of the statement before it**, so it
//< is writable in neither notation ("A bare block carries a label" in `../../../docs/DESIGN.md`).
//< `stmt` does not draw `stmt_block` (`../../kspl.kspeg`): the parse stops at the `{`.
// EXPECT: a bare block carries a label
fn main(): I32 {
  before: I32 = 1;
  {
    before += 1;
  }
  return before - 2;
}
